  "intro": "<p>Detached houses across the municipalities of Halkidiki: sea-view houses in Kassandra and Sithonia, quieter houses near Mount Athos and family homes close to Thessaloniki in Nea Propontida. Each listing shows the facts a buyer asks first: plot size, distance to the sea and pool.</p>",
  "body": "<h2>Detached houses by area</h2><p>Most houses for sale are on the two western peninsulas. In <strong>Kassandra</strong> they are close to the big beaches and the resorts of Sani, Possidi and Pefkochori. In <strong>Sithonia</strong> they sit among the pines above small coves, often with a view of Mount Athos. In <strong>Aristotelis</strong>, on the eastern side, the same budget buys a larger house or plot, often with a sea view. <strong>Nea Propontida</strong>, 40 to 60 km from Thessaloniki airport, and <strong>Polygyros</strong>, the regional capital, suit a family home used all year.</p><h2>Detached house, maisonette or apartment?</h2><p>A detached house stands on its own plot, with the most space and privacy. A maisonette gives you more space and privacy than an apartment, usually at a lower price than a detached house, and an apartment is the most affordable way to own a home here.</p><h2>What a detached house costs</h2><p>Detached houses start at about €200,000 near Thessaloniki; sea-view houses on Kassandra and Sithonia usually start at €500,000. The prices of the houses for sale today are shown with the list below.</p><h2>Letting a house near the beach</h2><p>Near the beach, a house lets for 16 to 20 weeks a year in Kassandra, the strongest rental market in Halkidiki.</p><h2>Buying a house from abroad</h2><p>Buying from abroad is common: you need a Greek tax number and a lawyer, viewings can be in person or by video call, and the deed can be signed with a power of attorney. Count 4 to 8 weeks in total and about 6% on top of the price for taxes and fees.</p>",
